---
import ScrollLayout from '../../layouts/ScrollLayout.astro';

// Copy is verbatim from github.com/The-Forest-Network/the-forest-network-web/issues/6
// (comment 5650893669, compiled by wandatree from the original trial-village
// invite + subsequent discussion). Do not edit the wording here without
// updating that issue.
//
// Background images are PLACEHOLDERS (site's existing forest.jpg, reused
// across all three sections with different overlay treatments) pending real
// photography for each section — see issue #6.
---

<ScrollLayout title="Join the Village">
  <div class="page-bg"></div>
  <a href="/" class="wordmark">The Forest Network</a>

  <section id="poem" class="screen screen--poem">
    <div class="overlay"></div>
    <div class="content">
      <p class="poem">
        we need but a place<br />
        to come back to<br />
        every so often;<br />
        a small home for us<br />
        to come together;<br />
        the relief of breathing<br />
        as one, for a while,<br />
        holding and being held;<br />
        humming, too, as one<br />
        until we remember<br />
        who we are, or could be.<br />
        so that we can fly off<br />
        again, out into the world<br />
        where things are now<br />
        so achingly, unnervingly,<br />
        coming apart.
      </p>
      <p class="attribution">Moon Song, &ldquo;the starling box&rdquo;</p>
    </div>
    <a href="#calling" class="scroll-cue" aria-label="Continue to the next section">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section id="calling" class="screen screen--calling">
    <div class="overlay"></div>
    <div class="content">
      <p>
        The Earth has been calling her human children to remember how to be in relation 
        to all things; to be in deep relation to ourselves and other human beings
        and the more-than-human beings we share this corner of the galaxy with.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Forest Network is a place where you can connect across the galaxies.
        It is a place in which you can seek solace;
        a place where you can deepen into the Mystery&hellip; with others.
        Where you can dream and explore all that is and all that can be.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Village will be unintentional, it will be uncertain, allowing new forms
        of being to arise; it is a place where villagers are open to the eddies of mystery;
        where we can allow the Village itself to be a participating being
        in the creation of the village tapestry within the global tapestry.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a href="#invitation" class="scroll-cue" aria-label="Continue to the next section">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section id="invitation" class="screen screen--invitation">
    <div class="overlay"></div>
    <div class="content content--wide">
      <p>
        If this invitation calls to your heart, please share with us what&rsquo;s drawing you
        through the fungal hyphae and into The Forest Network, and a little about yourself and
        your journey to date so that we can get to know you better. Here&rsquo;s a few ideas:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Poetry that expresses something deep inside</li>
        <li>Experiences you&rsquo;ve had in nature</li>
        <li>Dreams</li>
        <li>Art</li>
        <li>Imagery</li>
        <li>Recorded video/audio</li>
        <li>Collages</li>
        <li>Photographs</li>
        <li>Your deepest desires and fears</li>
        <li>Work you&rsquo;ve done in nature (rituals, remembrances, awakenings, healing, etc.)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Also include a paragraph expressing what you hope to find in the clearing created by
        The Forest Network Village.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please be concise, you are making your first introduction to the Village. We suggest
        what fits into 5 minutes of reading/listening/looking &mdash; eg 2 pages of written
        text, 5 minutes of audio, 2 images&hellip; Once you are part of the Village you will
        have ample opportunity to share as much as you wish.
      </p>
      <p>All submissions will be held close to our hearts and in strict confidence!</p>
      <p>If you have any questions, please don&rsquo;t hesitate to write.</p>
      <a
        class="write-link"
        href="mailto:trailhead@theforestnetwork.earth?subject=Join%20the%20Village"
        >Write to trailhead@theforestnetwork.earth</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</ScrollLayout>

<style>
  .wordmark {
    position: fixed;
    top: 1.75rem;
    left: 1.75rem;
    z-index: 10;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #c8dca0;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-shadow: 0 1px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);
    opacity: 0.85;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }
  .wordmark:hover {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .page-bg {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    background: url('/forest.jpg') center center / cover no-repeat;
  }

  .screen {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 100vh;
    min-height: 100svh;
    min-height: var(--app-vh, 100svh);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem;
    scroll-margin-top: 0;
  }

  .overlay {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
  }

  .screen--poem .overlay {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.62) 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.42) 50%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.67) 100%);
  }
  .screen--calling .overlay {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(6, 14, 4, 0.79) 0%, rgba(6, 14, 4, 0.57) 50%, rgba(6, 14, 4, 0.82) 100%);
  }
  .screen--invitation .overlay {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(4, 9, 3, 0.89) 0%, rgba(4, 9, 3, 0.75) 50%, rgba(4, 9, 3, 0.92) 100%);
  }

  .content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 42rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .content--wide {
    max-width: 38rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .poem {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.1vw, 1.4rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #f0f7e6;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .attribution {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.1vw, 1.4rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #f0f7e6;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
  }

  .screen--calling .content p {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.9vw, 1.3rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: #e6efd8;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }
  .screen--calling .content p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .screen--invitation .content p {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.6vw, 1.25rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #dbe6c8;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
    margin-bottom: 1.35rem;
  }

  .screen--invitation ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.35rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.6vw, 1.25rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: #dbe6c8;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
  }

  .write-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: #f0f7e6;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(168, 196, 128, 0.6);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
  }
  .write-link:hover {
    color: #c8dca0;
    border-bottom-color: rgba(200, 220, 160, 0.9);
  }

  .scroll-cue {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 1.5rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    z-index: 1;
    color: #c8dca0;
    opacity: 0.85;
    animation: nudge 2.4s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  .scroll-cue:hover {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  @keyframes nudge {
    0%,
    100% {
      transform: translate(-50%, 0);
    }
    50% {
      transform: translate(-50%, 8px);
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .scroll-cue {
      animation: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .screen {
      padding: 3.5rem 1.25rem;
    }
    .wordmark {
      top: 1.25rem;
      left: 1.25rem;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // CSS *vh/dvh/svh units were unreliable in testing on real mobile Safari —
  // sections rendered taller than the actually-visible area, leaving gaps
  // before the down-arrow / next section's content. window.innerHeight has
  // always correctly reflected the current visible viewport (toolbar state
  // included), so measure it directly instead.
  function setViewportHeight() {
    document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--app-vh', `${window.innerHeight}px`);
  }
  setViewportHeight();
  window.addEventListener('resize', setViewportHeight);
  window.addEventListener('orientationchange', setViewportHeight);
</script>
